    "summary": "High‑energy set with stellar Bird Song, Stella Blue and soaring solos",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a punchy first half highlighted by a gorgeous Bird Song and heartfelt Stella Blue. The second set builds momentum with Mississippi Half‑Step, China Cat > I Know You Rider and an emotional Morning Dew. Overall the performance is tight and inspired despite a few tape quirks.",
    "review": "July 22, 1972 at Seattle's Paramount Northwest Theater finds the Dead in fine summer form. Jerry rides his guitar like a storyteller, especially on Mississippi Half‑Step Uptown Toodeloo and the soaring Bird Song where his leads cut cleanly through the mix. Phil’s baritone vocals add depth to the ballads while also keeping the humor alive between numbers. Bob erupts with a five‑alarm fire on Yellow Dog in the audience tapes, but even on the soundboard releases his rhythm work drives the jams forward, particularly during China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider and the climactic Morning Dew. Keith’s keyboards weave texture throughout, from playful flourishes on the early cuts to supportive pads that lift the second‑set improvisations. Bill keeps the groove locked in, anchoring the high‑energy peaks with crisp, responsive drumming. Though a few early songs are missing or suffer tape hiccups, the setlist flows well and the energy stays consistently high, making this one of the stronger summer ’72 outings.",
